On Friday, June 29, 2012 6:22:17 PM UTC-7, David Melik wrote:
> I installed NetHack by using SBopkg (which downloads official source) on
> Slackware 13.37. However, whether I have num lock on or off, I cannot
> use the number pad for movement. I do not want to have to use rogue-like
> commands. Is there something special you have to do to the source on
> GNU/Linux to make the number pad work?

     The answer to this is essentially the same as to
the one you had about color.  Both number_pad and color
are disabled by default, but the Windows distribution(s)
include a sample configuration file which enables them,
so many players assume they're enabled by default.

     You need to set up a configuration file (or use
an environment variable) which specifies the option
settings you want.  On linux that file is ~/.nethackrc
(which is a file named ".nethackrc" in your home
directory, unlike Windows, which uses one callled
defaults.nh in nethack's directory).

     Put

OPTIONS=color,number_pad

in that file.  You probably also want IBMgraphics (might
not work without some fiddling) or DECgraphics (should
work straight off in xterm and other terminal emulators;
I'm not sure about displaying directory to the console).


